# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Note:** CPU time is the post-processing time. The three mirror circuits were submitted together in one run, so the recorded QPU and CPU times are for all three circuits together. Each Clifford circuit run contained nine PUBs with different circuit depths, so the recorded times are for all nine PUBs together. Each Ising circuit run contained 10 PUBs with different numbers of Trotter steps, so the recorded times are for all 10 PUBs together.\n"
msgstr "**Tandaan:** Ang CPU time ay ang oras ng post-processing. Magkakasamang isinumite sa isang run ang tatlong mirror circuit, kaya ang naitalang QPU at CPU time ay para sa lahat ng tatlong circuit nang magkakasama. Ang bawat run ng Clifford circuit ay may siyam na PUB na may iba't ibang circuit depth, kaya ang naitalang oras ay para sa lahat ng siyam na PUB nang magkakasama. Ang bawat run ng Ising circuit ay may 10 PUB na may iba't ibang bilang ng Trotter step, kaya ang naitalang oras ay para sa lahat ng 10 PUB nang magkakasama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the mirror circuits, the benchmarks use the RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal, and EfficientSU2 ansätze with 30, 35, and 40 qubits, respectively. The observables consist of a single Pauli-$Z$ operator on a randomly selected qubit, with an ideal expectation value of 1.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga mirror circuit, gumagamit ang mga benchmark ng mga ansatz na RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal, at EfficientSU2 na may 30, 35, at 40 qubit, ayon sa pagkakasunod. Binubuo ang mga observable ng iisang Pauli-$Z$ operator sa isang random na napiling qubit, na may ideal na expectation value na 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the Clifford circuits, the benchmarks use 50- and 100-qubit circuits with observables initialized as one or more randomly positioned Pauli-$Z$ operators. Operator evolution increases the Pauli weight of these observables, which provides more complex observables for benchmarking. The observables are constructed to have an ideal expectation value of 1, which is independently verified with stabilizer simulation.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga Clifford circuit, gumagamit ang mga benchmark ng mga circuit na may 50 at 100 qubit na may mga observable na sinimulan bilang isa o higit pang random na nakaposisyong Pauli-$Z$ operator. Pinapataas ng operator evolution ang Pauli weight ng mga observable na ito, na nagbibigay ng mas masalimuot na mga observable para sa benchmarking. Binuo ang mga observable para magkaroon ng ideal na expectation value na 1, na hiwalay na beneripika gamit ang stabilizer simulation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the Trotterized 2D tilted-field Ising (TFI) Hamiltonian simulations, the benchmarks use three parameter regimes: small angle $(\\theta_X,\\theta_Z,\\theta_{ZZ})=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, near-Clifford $(0.1,0.05,1.5708)$, and chaotic $(0.53,0.1,1.0)$. The observable is the average magnetization,\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga simulation ng Trotterized 2D tilted-field Ising (TFI) Hamiltonian, gumagamit ang mga benchmark ng tatlong parameter regime: small angle $(\\theta_X,\\theta_Z,\\theta_{ZZ})=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, near-Clifford $(0.1,0.05,1.5708)$, at chaotic $(0.53,0.1,1.0)$. Ang observable ay ang average magnetization,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O_M = \\frac{1}{M}\\sum_i Z_i,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O_M = \\frac{1}{M}\\sum_i Z_i,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $M$ is the number of qubits in the simulation. Ideal expectation values are computed with sparse Pauli dynamics (SPD), a Pauli propagation method, and are validated against Qiskit statevector simulations for circuits with fewer than 29 qubits.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $M$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit sa simulation. Kinakalkula ang mga ideal na expectation value gamit ang sparse Pauli dynamics (SPD), isang Pauli propagation method, at bineberipika laban sa mga Qiskit statevector simulation para sa mga circuit na wala pang 29 qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For all benchmarks, mitigation accuracy is calculated as\n"
msgstr "Para sa lahat ng benchmark, kinakalkula ang mitigation accuracy bilang\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Accuracy}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Accuracy}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\left(\n"
"1-\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\left|\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}-\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}\\right|\n"
"}{\n"
"\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}\n"
"}\n"
"\\right)\\times100\\%,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\left(\n"
"1-\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\left|\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}-\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}\\right|\n"
"}{\n"
"\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}\n"
"}\n"
"\\right)\\times100\\%,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}$ and $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}$ are the ideal and mitigated expectation values, respectively.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}}$ at $\\langle O\\rangle_{\\mathrm{mitigated}}$ ay ang ideal at mitigated na expectation value, ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get support {#get-support}"
msgstr "Humingi ng suporta {#get-support}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The AI-QEM support team is here to help. If you encounter any issues, have questions about using the AI-QEM Function, or need help troubleshooting a job, contact the support team.\n"
msgstr "Nandito ang AI-QEM support team para tumulong. Kung may makaharap kang mga isyu, may mga tanong tungkol sa paggamit ng AI-QEM Function, o kailangan mo ng tulong sa pag-troubleshoot ng job, makipag-ugnayan sa support team.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support: quantumfunction.support@ltm.com\n"
msgstr "Suporta: quantumfunction.support@ltm.com\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To help the support team investigate and resolve your issue as quickly as possible, include the following information in your support request:\n"
msgstr "Para matulungan ang support team na imbestigahan at lutasin ang isyu mo nang mabilis hangga't maaari, isama ang sumusunod na impormasyon sa support request mo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function job ID (for example, `job.job_id`)\n"
msgstr "Job ID ng Function (halimbawa, `job.job_id`)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A detailed description of the issue\n"
msgstr "Detalyadong paglalarawan ng isyu\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any relevant error messages, stack traces, or error codes\n"
msgstr "Anumang kaugnay na error message, stack trace, o error code\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expected behavior and actual behavior (if applicable)\n"
msgstr "Inaasahang gawi at aktwal na gawi (kung naaangkop)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Complete information helps the support team diagnose issues more efficiently and resolve them faster.\n"
msgstr "Nakakatulong ang kumpletong impormasyon para mas mahusay na ma-diagnose ng support team ang mga isyu at mas mabilis itong malutas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The AI-QEM support team also welcomes feedback and feature requests. If you have suggestions for improvements or capabilities that you want to see in future releases, send them to quantumfunction.support@ltm.com.\n"
msgstr "Malugod ding tinatanggap ng AI-QEM support team ang feedback at mga feature request. Kung may mga mungkahi ka para sa mga pagpapabuti o kakayahang gusto mong makita sa mga susunod na release, ipadala ang mga ito sa quantumfunction.support@ltm.com.\n"

